[center][size=6][b]Ragdoll Together[/b][/size]
[size=4]Ragdoll Physics Sync for Skyrim Together Reborn[/size][/center]

Everyone sees the same fall. When a player or an NPC is knocked down, flung by a shout, killed or knocked out in [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b], the body falls, bounces, comes to rest and gets up on every screen exactly as it does for the player who controls it, instead of lying stiff or in a T-pose on everyone else's.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The whole ragdoll is shared[/b]: the fall, every bounce, arms and hands, and where the body comes to rest.
[*][b]The get-up too[/b]: the body follows its owner's get-up until the actor is back on its feet, then blends back to its own animation.
[*][b]Players and NPCs[/b]: whoever controls an actor in Skyrim Together decides how it falls; everyone else sees that.
[*][b]Bodies at rest stay put[/b]: also for players who arrive later or come back into range.
[*][b]Smooth on other screens[/b]: played back slightly behind, in step with the character's movement, so a late packet doesn't make the body jitter.
[*][b]Works with the official Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.3[/b] from Nexus: the main file (Skyrim [b]1.7.104[/b]) and the optional file for [b]1.6.1170 / 1.6.1179[/b].
[*][b]Also works with Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.5[/b] (absol89), including its [b]1.5.97[/b] port.
[*][b]No server changes[/b]: it plays on any regular server of your Skyrim Together version.
[*][b]Plays nicely with SkyParkour Together, RaceMenu Together and LipSync Together[/b]: our mods share one launcher, so you can run them together.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Every player in the session[/b] needs all of these:
[list]
[*]Skyrim Special/Anniversary Edition [b]1.5.97, 1.6.1170, 1.6.1179 or 1.7.104[/b]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] for your game version
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url] [b]1.8.3[/b] (the Nexus main or optional file for your game version), or Skyrim Together Reborn [b]1.8.5[/b]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Which Skyrim Together do I have?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.8.3 (official)[/b]: you downloaded Skyrim Together Reborn from its Nexus page. Main file = Skyrim 1.7.104; optional file "for 1.6.1170" = Skyrim 1.6.1170/1.6.1179. [b]Not sure? This is you.[/b]
[*][b]1.8.5[/b]: you use absol89's 1.8.5 build, or play on Skyrim 1.5.97 with the 1.5.97 port.
[/list]
1.8.3 and 1.8.5 can't join each other's servers, so everyone in your session needs the same one.

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Skyrim Together only starts when its launcher sits in the same folder as the rest of Skyrim Together ([font=Courier New]libcef.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]EarlyLoad.dll[/font], the UI...). How you get this mod's launcher there depends on your mod manager.
[list=1]
[*]Install Skyrim Together Reborn as usual.
[*]Install this mod. The installer asks which Skyrim Together you use, then your game version.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Mod Organizer 2[/b][/size]
MO2 starts a launcher from its real folder on disk, so mod order is not enough. Copy the launcher once:
[list=1]
[*]Right-click [b]Ragdoll Together[/b] > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]Right-click your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] mod > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]In the Skyrim Together folder, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] to [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] (your backup).
[*]Copy [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the Ragdoll Together folder into the Skyrim Together folder. On [b]1.5.97[/b], also copy [font=Courier New]EarlyLoad.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]TPProcess.exe[/font] and [font=Courier New]versionlib-ae-to-se-1-5-97-0.map[/font].
[*]Keep Ragdoll Together enabled (it provides the SKSE plugin) and start the game with your usual MO2 entry for Skyrim Together, the one pointing into the Skyrim Together Reborn mod. [b]Don't[/b] point an MO2 entry at the Ragdoll Together folder: the launcher can't start from there and simply closes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Vortex[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Set Ragdoll Together to load [b]after[/b] Skyrim Together Reborn and deploy.
[*]Start the game from [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] as you normally start Skyrim Together.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Is it working?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/RagdollTogether.log[/font] says [i]"Skyrim Together add-on found"[/i].
[*]Skyrim Together's log ([font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/logs[/font]) contains [i]"Ragdoll Together: Ragdoll Together 1.0.0 found; ragdolls are shared"[/i].
[/list]
[b]The launcher closes straight away[/b] (no window, no log): it was started from a folder without the rest of Skyrim Together. In MO2, do the copy steps above.
[b]The SKSE log says the add-on was not found:[/b] the game started with a different [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font]. In MO2, check the copied launcher is the one in the Skyrim Together Reborn mod; in Vortex, check the load order.
[b]A body still lies stiff for you:[/b] the player who controls it doesn't have Ragdoll Together, or uses a different launcher.

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]
Skyrim Together runs an actor's physics only on the PC that controls it, so everyone else sees a stiff body. This mod has two parts:
[list]
[*][b]RagdollTogether.dll[/b] (SKSE plugin): switches the add-on on and writes a log. It reads no game memory, so one DLL works on every game version.
[*][b]SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] for your Skyrim Together and game version: that exact Skyrim Together release with our small add-ons. Ragdoll Together's reads where the ragdoll's bodies are on the controlling player's screen, sends them compactly through Skyrim Together's existing relay, and puts the body in that pose on everyone else's screen as the frame is drawn. It is the same launcher our other mods ship, so they never fight over it. Nothing else in Skyrim Together is changed.
[/list]
Skyrim Together's server keeps every relayed message until it restarts. Ragdoll Together only sends while a body moves, roughly 15-30 KB per knockdown or death; on a very long, combat-heavy session that adds up to some tens of MB per PC, cleared when the server restarts.

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]SkyParkour Together, RaceMenu Together, LipSync Together[/b]: fully compatible. All ship the identical launcher carrying every add-on, so install them in any order. Keep them up to date together.
[*][b]Other mods that replace or patch SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] (other Skyrim Together forks, STRPluginMessagingAPI) conflict with this mod: only one launcher can be used.
[*]Our separate [b]Combined test build[/b] (Parkour + RaceMenu + Ragdoll) has its own ragdoll sync; don't use both.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
[b]MO2:[/b] delete the copied [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the Skyrim Together Reborn mod, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] back, then remove this mod. [b]Vortex:[/b] remove the mod.

